# hip_bright.tsv

Dataset: star-hip — Hipparcos main catalogue: the 960 stars brighter than V = 4.55 that have a
  position and six fast-moving stars, positions (ICRS, epoch J1991.25) and proper motions
File: data/star/hip/raw/hip_bright.tsv
SHA-256: 9ca0b2df5f5129d70b7fcbf48eb03b3afffdce4121d69c8587b3a810b8b1593f (also in
  data/star/hip/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/star/hip && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: no, only this description and the hash: CDS/VizieR distributes it free for
  scientific use with citation; its terms do not say that a copy may be republished, so only the
  hash and the request are given. Get it from
  https://vizier.cfa.harvard.edu/viz-bin/asu-tsv?-source=I/239/hip_main&-out=HIP,Vmag,RAICRS,DEICRS,Plx,pmRA,pmDE,B-V&Vmag=%3C4.55&-out.max=3000&-sort=HIP
  (or fog fetch star-hip), then compare its SHA-256 with the one above.
Obtained: the answer of a public web API to the request given.
From: VizieR I/239 (Hipparcos main catalogue), Harvard mirror, the request in the URL; the file's
  header carries the request and its date.
URL:
  https://vizier.cfa.harvard.edu/viz-bin/asu-tsv?-source=I/239/hip_main&-out=HIP,Vmag,RAICRS,DEICRS,Plx,pmRA,pmDE,B-V&Vmag=%3C4.55&-out.max=3000&-sort=HIP
Collected: 2026-11-11
Licence: other — The Hipparcos and Tycho Catalogues (ESA 1997), distributed by the CDS (VizieR
  I/239), free for scientific use with citation.
Sources:
- ESA, The Hipparcos and Tycho Catalogues, ESA SP-1200 (1997); VizieR I/239, table hip_main
  <https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/cat/I/239>
Evidence class (rule 10): measure
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): Angles between the same stars that change with the
  observer's place or with the hour of the night, as lights on a dome a few thousand kilometres up
  would show.
Built by: fog build star-hip
Generated files:
- src/data/presets/star-hip.js
Code:
- tools/internal/build/starhip
- src/tabs/star/radec-logic.js
Shown on the page:
- #tab-star/sky-h2a
- #tab-star/sky-h2b
- #tab-star/sky-h2c
Notes: Two of the 962 bright entries (HIP 55203 and 78727, close binaries) have no astrometric
  solution in the main catalogue and are left out. Nothing is computed by the build: the rows are
  copied as published, rounded to 1e-5 deg and 0.1 mas/yr. The page moves the stars itself
  (src/tabs/star/radec-logic.js): proper motion along a straight line with no radial velocity,
  precession as a rotation about the pole of the ecliptic. The two files are VizieR answers (Harvard
  mirror; the CDS server was down on the day), their headers carry the request and its date.

Written by `fog build explain` from data/star/hip/dataset.json and data/star/hip/inputs.lock: edit those, not this file.
